Description: thread-safe group enumeration
 glibc's getgrouplist() and initgroups() walk the module's group entries
 with setgrent/getgrent_r/endgrent from whatever thread calls them. One
 static FILE and fgetgrent()'s static buffer were shared by every thread:
 configd, which calls getgrouplist() from many goroutines, died with SIGSEGV
 and lost every configuration session. The stream and line buffer are now
 per thread (fgetgrent_r), and configuration parsing, which rewrites the
 server tables, is serialised. test/grent_threads (make check) runs eight
 concurrent enumerations; it segfaulted before this change.
Author: NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-09
---
